Long lecture videos are hard to navigate. A student may need one specific explanation inside a one-hour or two-hour video. If the video has no accurate chapters, the student must manually search through the video. LECSEG tries to predict topic boundaries automatically.

Evidence: `thesis/chapters/chapter1_introduction.tex`

### Type of Project

This is not an image-classification thesis. It is a **lecture-video topic segmentation** thesis using natural language processing, video/audio preprocessing, multimodal features, and segmentation metrics.

