We created a lecture segmentation research artifact, not just a written report. The repository contains a 30-video manifest, transcripts, sentence-split data, ground-truth chapter labels, reviewed hierarchical subtopic labels, multiple embedding folders, preprocessing code, segmentation algorithms, evaluation scripts, result JSON files, statistical tests, thesis tables, figures, paper draft, and defense materials. The code under `src/lecseg/` implements the core methods and metrics. The `results/` folder contains many experiments, including strong results and failed attempts. The thesis PDF and defense deck connect those results into a research story.

