## 7. Beginner Concepts Needed Before Understanding This Thesis

| Concept | Simple definition | Real-life example | Why it matters | Viva explanation |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Lecture video | A recorded class or tutorial | A YouTube university lecture | The data type | "Our input is long educational video." |
| Transcript | Written version of speech | Subtitles of a lecture | The system mainly reads text | "We convert speech to text first." |
| Sentence | A single complete statement | "Now we define entropy." | Boundary positions are between sentences | "Sentence is the unit of prediction." |
| Topic boundary | Where one topic ends and another starts | Moving from definition to examples | Main target | "We predict these boundary points." |
| Chapter | Large topic section | "Linear regression" in a lecture | Main evaluation level | "Chapters are coarse sections." |
| Subtopic | Smaller topic inside a chapter | "Gradient descent intuition" | Hierarchical output | "Subtopics are finer divisions." |
| Embedding | Numbers representing meaning | A sentence turned into coordinates | Main feature | "Similar sentences have similar vectors." |
| Cosine similarity | Measures direction similarity between vectors | Two arrows pointing same way | Detects meaning changes | "A drop suggests topic shift." |
| Baseline | Simple comparison method | Starting score to beat | Needed for research | "We compare against established methods." |
| Evaluation metric | A number measuring quality | Exam score | Proves method performance | "Pk and WD are our main scores." |
| Pk | Window-based segmentation error | Checks if two nearby points belong to same topic | Main metric | "Lower Pk is better." |
| WindowDiff | Counts boundary number mismatch in windows | Checks whether a window has correct boundary count | Main metric | "Lower WD is better." |
| F1 | Balance of precision and recall | How many hits were correct and found | Exact boundary view | "Higher F1 is better." |
| Bootstrap CI | Re-sampling to estimate uncertainty | Rechecking score many times with shuffled samples | Makes small dataset claims honest | "We report confidence intervals." |
| Wilcoxon test | Statistical paired comparison | Checks if method A usually beats method B | Validates improvement | "It tests whether gains are likely real." |
| Oracle | Impossible best chooser used for diagnosis | A teacher tells the system the best choice | Shows potential headroom | "Oracle is not deployable." |
| LOO selector | Leave-one-video-out method selector | Train on 29 videos, test on 1 | Best deployable local result | "It avoids testing on training video." |

