## 10. Preprocessing Pipeline and Theory

Preprocessing means converting raw lecture videos into clean, structured data that the algorithms can use.

### Actual Preprocessing Steps

| Step | Where found | What it does | Input | Output | Why used | Risk/downside |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Video/audio download | `scripts/download_all.py`, `data/raw/` | Downloads lecture media | YouTube URL | MP4/WAV/media files | Needed for ASR and visual features | Copyright/release limitations |
| Transcription | `scripts/transcribe.py`, `scripts/vast_transcribe.py`, `data/transcripts/` | Converts speech to text | Audio/video | transcript JSON/TXT | Main input for text segmentation | ASR errors |
| Sentence splitting | `src/lecseg/preprocess/sentence_split.py` | Splits transcript into sentence records | Whisper segments | `sentences.json` | Boundaries predicted between sentences | Timestamp approximation |
| Shot detection | `src/lecseg/preprocess/shot_detection.py`, `data/shots/` | Detects visual cuts | Video | shot JSON | Visual boundary cue | Lectures may have few shots |
| OCR | `src/lecseg/preprocess/ocr.py`, `data/ocr/` | Reads slide text | Keyframes | OCR JSON/text | Slide topic cue | Noisy OCR, not useful for chalkboard |
| Prosody | `src/lecseg/preprocess/prosody.py`, `data/prosody/` | Extracts pauses and pitch | Audio/transcript | prosody JSON | Speaker transition cue | Often subtopic-level, may hurt chapter Pk |
| Embedding generation | `src/lecseg/features/text_embeddings.py`, `data/embeddings/` | Converts sentences to vectors | Sentences | `.npy` arrays | Meaning representation | Model choice affects quality |
| Alignment | `src/lecseg/features/alignment.py` | Aligns modalities to sentence timeline | time features | feature matrix | Fusion needs same timeline | Timing mismatch |

### Simple Flow Diagram

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[YouTube lecture video] --> B[Audio transcription with Whisper]
    B --> C[Sentence splitting with spaCy]
    C --> D[Sentence timeline]
    D --> E[Text embeddings]
    A --> F[Shot detection / OCR / CLIP]
    A --> G[Prosody pause and pitch]
    E --> H[Boundary scoring]
    F --> H
    G --> H
    H --> I[Predicted topic boundaries]
    I --> J[Evaluation against YouTube chapters]
```

### Why Raw Data Is Not Directly Usable

Raw video is too complex for direct comparison. The system needs text, timestamps, vectors, and aligned features. Without preprocessing, the algorithm would not know where sentences begin, what each sentence means, or how to compare predicted boundaries to ground truth.

Evidence: `src/lecseg/preprocess/`, `src/lecseg/features/`

### Most Important Preprocessing Step

Sentence splitting and text embeddings are the most important for final results because the best official methods rely primarily on text embedding boundary signals.

Evidence: `results/eval_bge.json`, `results/eval_alignment_sweep.json`

