## 15. Metrics and Evaluation Used With Theory

| Metric/evaluation | Meaning | Why used | How to read | Good value | Bad value | Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Pk | Window-based segmentation error | Standard topic segmentation metric | Lower is better | 0 is perfect | Near 1 bad | `src/lecseg/metrics.py` |
| WindowDiff | Counts boundary-count mismatch in a window | Penalizes segmentation structure errors | Lower is better | 0 perfect | high bad | `src/lecseg/metrics.py` |
| Boundary Similarity | Boundary-level similarity with near-match scoring | Shows boundary closeness | Higher is better | 1 perfect | 0 bad | `src/lecseg/metrics.py` |
| Tolerance-F1 / F1@2 | Predicted boundary counts correct if within 2 sentences | Exact boundary-hit view | Higher is better | 1 perfect | 0 bad | `src/lecseg/metrics.py` |
| Precision | Of predicted boundaries, how many were correct | Avoid false positives | Higher better | 1 perfect | 0 bad | `src/lecseg/metrics.py` |
| Recall | Of true boundaries, how many were found | Avoid missed boundaries | Higher better | 1 perfect | 0 bad | `src/lecseg/metrics.py` |
| H-WD | Hierarchical WindowDiff | Subtopic-aware evaluation | Lower better | 0 perfect | high bad | `src/lecseg/metrics.py` |
| Cohen's kappa | Agreement between annotators beyond chance | Label reliability | Higher better | 1 perfect | 0 chance | `scripts/compute_iaa.py`, `data/gt_hier/iaa_report.json` |
| Bootstrap CI | Confidence interval from resampling videos | Shows uncertainty | Narrower is more stable | NA | NA | `src/lecseg/eval/stats.py` |
| Wilcoxon test | Paired statistical test | Checks significance | p < 0.05 often significant | low p | high p | `results/method_selector_significance.json` |

### How to Compare Results Fairly

Use Pk and WD as the primary segmentation-window metrics. Use F1@2 as complementary exact-boundary evidence. Do not say a method is universally better if it improves Pk but worsens F1, or improves F1 but worsens Pk/WD. This thesis has exactly that tradeoff.

Evidence: `thesis/chapters/chapter4_results.tex`

